NAME
    units - the catalogue of test units, one per line

SYNOPSIS
    units [--kind cargo|dotnet] [--tier T] [--crates] [--rev REV] [--repo DIR]
    units --key UNIT [--profile P] [--rev REV] [--repo DIR]

DESCRIPTION
    A command of the emusen.testing module, the testing studio. A unit is
    the smallest thing the studio runs and records as a whole. It is
    derived from the revision's files, never from a hand-kept list:

        cargo    a Cargo root: a crate outside any workspace, or a
                 workspace, counted once (Platform); --crates adds a
                 workspace's member crates as 'crate' lines
        dotnet   a test class of a test project (a project that
                 references xunit), found in its sources: a class with
                 [Fact] or [Theory] tests of its own, merged across
                 partial files, or one inheriting an abstract class's
                 tests; and 'lunap', the sibling toolkit's suite

    Each line is tab-separated: kind, unit, tier tag, needs. The tier tag
    is 'nightly' for a class carrying [Trait("Category", "nightly")] and
    'land' otherwise.

    --key prints a unit's key and what it is made of: the git object name
    of every input folder (the unit's own, the crates and projects it is
    built from, its workspace's manifest and lock, the declared extras of
    Testing/inputs.json), the toolchain (rustc -V or dotnet --version),
    the profile, ~/.cargo/config.toml for a cargo unit and the LunaP
    checkout's commit for a dotnet one. The key is git's hash of those
    lines. When an input has uncommitted changes the answer is 'none' and
    the status 1: git's objects would not describe what runs, so nothing
    may be reused for it.

    The repository is --repo, else EMUSEN_REPO, else the one holding the
    working folder. Revisions are read from git objects, so a branch need
    not be checked out. See EmuSen_Testing.md §3.1.

EXAMPLES
    units --kind cargo | wc -l
    units --tier nightly
    units --crates | grep '^crate' | grep Platform/
    units --key "cargo:EmuSen/Cores/Sony/Sapphire - PlayStation 2"
